 ## Overview
-Physical Parameter Optimization replaces the standard spherical harmonic (SH) color and empirical opacity attributes of 3D Gaussian Splatting with a set of physical quantities representing a participating medium [S1, unofficial]. This allows for real-time rendering and dynamic relighting (arbitrary sun direction) by solving the radiative transfer equation through the Gaussian primitives rather than approximating lighting with SH coefficients [S1, unofficial]. It is distinct from standard 3DGS training by optimizing extinction, albedo, and scattering asymmetry instead of color and opacity [S1, unofficial].
+Physical Parameter Optimization replaces the standard spherical harmonic (SH) color and empirical opacity attributes of 3D Gaussian Splatting with a set of physical quantities representing a participating medium [S1, unofficial]. This substitution enables real-time rendering and dynamic relighting under arbitrary sun directions by solving the radiative transfer equation directly through the Gaussian primitives [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard 3DGS training by optimizing extinction, albedo, and scattering asymmetry rather than approximating lighting with empirical color coefficients [S1, unofficial].
 
